e  so we are really excited to be working  with Cornell Cooperative Extension at  Wyoming County and other partners to  pilot some trainings technical  assistance and communications activities  are gated towards women landowners as  well as farmers in the Genesee River  watershed and we've been doing that for  the last two years  experimenting with some different  approaches over the next year we're  going to be sharing our results in what  we're learning about really think that  that is an important part of this  conversation that's often overlooked  because it's not just the farmer owned  land that rental land is a really  important piece of this conversation so  I get just want to close that this is a  really important conversation and it's  not a conversation though just for  farmers it's with farmers but really  this is a conversation for all New  Yorkers because you know for all of us  eaters all of us that are thinking about  the water we want to drink or the water  we want to swim in in the health of our  this is a conversation that's relevant  allmusic's so thank you very much this  has been a production of Cornell  University on the web at cornell edu
 

